   2086  fd39							; Door stripe color ($8D) is staged inside PhaseBlink (this window
   2087  fd39							; was full to the $F4C4 pin, retired 2026-10-20 — the 14B staging
   2088  fd39							; block lives with the walk where there is hole).
   2089  fd39							; --- Phase 3: phase-cell blink (PF buffer pokes) ----------------------
   2090  fd39							; Body moved after the level data (PhaseBlink, ~130B — the StageBandTab
   2091  fd39							; window $F3C4..$F4C4 was full; the data window has the only free
   2092  fd39							; hole). Contract: clobbers A/X/Y/FetchPtr/RectCount/LineCount/
   2093  fd39							; CollisionCellX/CollisionEndY ($8F scratch — the pack below rebuilds
   2094  fd39							; it). The PF buffers ARE the collision map (cell walk + laser read
   2095  fd39							; them) — toggling the cell's two bits THERE makes render + PHM +
   2096  fd39							; laser follow with zero kernel cost. 64f full cycle = EnemyRamP bit5
   2097  fd39							; (32 on + 32 off; clock-derived, no state bytes — locked plan).
   2098  fd39							; --- PhaseBlink ping-pong (chunk A2): it MUST run after the band/ball
   2099  fd39							; staging above and before the pack below (the crunch walk overwrites
   2100  fd39							; Temp/BandTab for its cell — running it earlier let SBT's own staging
   2101  fd39							; erase the crunch mask, and every crunch kill stopped latching).
   2102  fd39							; Leg 1: this `sta` runs here, the fetch at $F803 is bank2's
   2103  fd39							; `jmp PhBlinkTail` (byte-image pinned in bank2.asm).
   2104  fd39							; --- A3: PhaseBlink is LOCAL now (the record stream lives in bank3) ---
   2105  fd39		       20 d9 f9 	      jsr	PhaseBlink
   2106  fd3c				   SBT_B
   2107  fd3c							; --- Phase 4: pack collision overlay byte → CollisionEndY ($8F) ---
   2108  fd3c							; b4-b7 = right_col+1, b0-2 = ball band mask, b3 = M1 present
   2109  fd3c							; (staged $8E != 0), 0 = symmetric. Cave never
   2110  fd3c							; writes $8F; bank1 HUD entry copies it to LineCount ($84 — cave .Row
   2111  fd3c							; clobbers it) before overscan PHM reads. BallX in Temp stays raw (the
   2112  fd3c							; kernel's ball block reads it later this VBL).
   2113  fd3c							; b3 seeds BEFORE the Temp=0 early-out so an M1-ONLY room still packs
   2114  fd3c							; nonzero (kernel OverlayTramp gates on LineCount != 0 — no M1 cross
   2115  fd3c							; otherwise).
   2116  fd3c		       a5 8e		      lda	CollisionEndX	; staged M1X (kill-gated above)
   2117  fd3e		       f0 02		      beq	.M1nof	; 0 = no M1 → seed 0 (A is 0)
   2118  fd40		       a9 08		      lda	#$08	; b3 = M1 present
   2119  fd42				   .M1nof
